y works without containerization. I want to create a Docker container with this code but it looks like it stucks on *client.start function*. This is the container log:\r\n```\r\n2024-02-08 17:42:34 [2024-02-08T16:42:34.106] [INFO] - [Running gramJS version 2.19.9]\r\n2024-02-08 17:42:34 [2024-02-08T16:42:34.119] [INFO] - [Connecting to 91.108.56.132:80/TCPFull...]\r\n2024-02-08 17:42:34 [2024-02-08T16:42:34.125] [INFO] - [Connection to 91.108.56.132:80/TCPFull complete!]\r\n2024-02-08 17:42:34 [2024-02-08T16:42:34.134] [INFO] - [Using LAYER 166 for initial connect] \r\n```\r\n\r\nIt doesn't even print \"You should now be connected\".\r\nI took care of copying into the image also \"my_session\" in order to avoid the need to login again.\r\n\r\nThis is the Dockerfile:\r\n```\r\nFROM node:18-alpine\r\n\r\nWORKDIR /telegrambot\r\n\r\nCOPY ./bot.js ./package.json .\r\nCOPY ./my_session ./my_session\r\n\r\nRUN npm install\r\n\r\nCMD [ \"node\", \"bot.js\" ]\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat does it could be the problem?\r\n\r\nThank you in advance! ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/637/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/637/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/302","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/302/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/302/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gram-js/gramjs/issues/302/events","html_url":"https://github.com/gram-js/gramjs/issues/302","id":1209106351,"node_id":"I_kwDODAde7c5IEX-v","number":302,"title":"TIMEOUT I'm using version 2.6.13","user":{"login":"wind-hx","id":17685971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Njg1OTc